wrk:17694
    a rdac:C10001 ;
    rdaxd:P00018 "http://entedit.org/work/17694",
        "https://www.isfdb.org/cgi-bin/title.cgi?17694" ;
    rdawd:P10223 "Orphans of the Sky"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Orphans of the Sky (Heinlein, Robert A.)" ;
    rdawd:P10219 "1963-12" ;
    rdawd:P10330 "Centuries after a mutiny on a generational colony ship, most of the occupants believe the Ship is the whole world, and regard actual ship history as religious myth. Two populations now exist. The descendants of the \"Crew\" live on the normal gravity levels in a functioning society, growing crops and performing ship maintenance as religious rites. The \"muties\" (mutants and/or descendants of mutineers) live a marginal life in the increasingly lower gravity levels and practice cannibalism. When an intelligent mutant captures a young \"crewman\" alive, he begins to show him the truth about the Ship.\nReturning to Crew society, he and his friend expect to bring enlightenment to others and a return to the generation ship's purpose. A crafty political wannabe pledges to aid them, but instead uses them as fodder for his own goals. Hunted by police, they realize they must escape.",
        "This novel was first published in \"Astounding Science Fiction\" in 1941 as two separate novelettes: \"Universe\" and its sequel \"Common Sense\". \"Universe\" was reprinted by itself in book form in 1951. The two were combined to form \"Orphans of the Sky\" in 1963." ;
    entedit:P01 vtp:V1000 ;
    entedit:P02 ntsf:258 ;
    rdawo:P10061 per:29 .

