    rdawd:P10219 "1962-03-03" ;
    rdawd:P10330 "The Pacific Book of Australian SF gives the source of this story as \"The Bulletin\", an Australian national weekly.\nL. T. Sargent's \"Utopian Literature in English: An Annotated Bibliography from 1516 to the Present\" (https://openpublishing.psu.edu/utopia/content/it-could-be-you) gives the issue date as 3 March 1962\nMerril lists the source as Short Story International, which reprinted the story in the September, 1964 issue.\nThe MUP Encyclopaedia of Australian Science Fiction & Fantasy gives a 1962 first publication, in Hal Porter's Coast to Coast Sydney : Angus et Robertson, 1962, which volume credits \"The Bulletin\". OCLC 10209746" ;
