    rdawd:P10330 "A group of alien \"boy scouts\" is visiting a planet as corporeal beings. Usually they live on the upper atmosphere in a non-material state, but now they are living like their ancestors. One young scout is a bit timid, but the scout leader tells him that several bulls of the almost mythical beasts, Mirash, have been seen. Maybe he could redeem himself and hunt one of the beasts? At the same time, human prospectors are trying to find valuable jewels on the planet..." ;
    entedit:P01 vtp:V1000 ;
    entedit:P02 entedit:T02 ;
    rdawo:P10061 per:818 .

wrk:45874
    a rdac:C10001 ;
    rdaxd:P00018 "http://entedit.org/work/45874",
        "https://www.isfdb.org/cgi-bin/title.cgi?45874" ;
    rdawd:P10223 "A Ticket to Tranai"@en ;
    rdfs:label "A Ticket to Tranai (Sheckley, Robert)" ;
    rdawd:P10219 "1955-10" ;
    rdawd:P10330 "A man hears about a nice planet where life is really free. There are no taxes, there are ample opportunities for everyone, and all of the women are young and beautiful. But it turns out that there are some catches. And then some more catches. And then even more." ;
    entedit:P01 vtp:V1000 ;
    entedit:P02 entedit:T02 ;
    rdawo:P10061 per:818 .

wrk:45877
    a rdac:C10001 ;
    rdaxd:P00018 "http://entedit.org/work/45877",
        "https://www.isfdb.org/cgi-bin/title.cgi?45877" ;
    rdawd:P10223 "The Discovery of Morniel Mathaway"@en ;
    rdfs:label "The Discovery of Morniel Mathaway (Tenn, William)" ;
    rdawd:P10219 "1955-10" ;
    rdawd:P10330 "A mediocre artist and his friend survive mostly by shoplifting and living frugally. One day, a man appears from a hole in a wall of their room and announces that he had come from the future to meet the greatest artist that has ever lived. But he doesn't recognize any of the paintings the artist has at home, and they are not even close to the quality they are supposed to be." ;
    entedit:P01 vtp:V1000 ;
    entedit:P02 entedit:T02 ;
    rdawo:P10061 per:484 .

wrk:45879
    a rdac:C10001 ;
