    rdfs:label "The Last Flight of Dr. Ain (James Tiptree, Jr.)" ;
    rdawd:P10219 "1969-03" ;
    rdawd:P10330 "\"The Last Flight of Doctor Ain\" copyright © 1974 by Harry Harrison for SF: Author's Choice 4 (heavily revised version of original published in Galaxy for March 1969, © 1969 by Universal Publishing and Distributing Corporation) [source: Acknowledgments page of Warm Worlds and Otherwise)].\nOriginally written in 1968.\nThe \"Warm Worlds and Otherwise\" edition (1979 Del Rey/Ballantine), the \"Galaxy: Thirty Years of Innovative Science Fiction\" edition (1980 Playboy Press), the \"Yesterday's Tomorrows\" edition (1982 Berkley Books), the \"Her Smoke Rose Up Forever\" edition (1990 Arkham House), \"The Prentice Hall Anthology of Science Fiction and Fantasy\" edition (2003 Prentice-Hall), the \"From Here to Forever\" edition (2003 Scarecrow Press), \"The Vintage Book of American Women Writers\" edition (2011 Vintage Books), and the \"Women of Futures Past\" edition (2016 Baen) all use the revised text first published in the 1974 anthology \"SF: Author's Choice 4\". \"The Future Is Female!: 25 Classic Science Fiction Stories by Women, From Pulp Pioneers to Ursula K. Le Guin\" edition (2018 The Library of America) uses the original 1969 version published in Galaxy Magazine." ;
    entedit:P01 vtp:V1000 ;
    entedit:P02 entedit:T02 ;
    rdawo:P10061 per:57 .

