    rdawd:P10223 "The Year of the Jackpot"@en ;
    rdfs:label "The Year of the Jackpot (Heinlein, Robert A.)" ;
    rdawd:P10219 "1952-03" ;
    rdawd:P10330 "A statistician notes that the number of strange incidents are increasing. His work has always tracked events that occur cyclically; they increase to a maximum and then fall to a minimum, and knows that different types have different periodic cycles: some may be every 18 years, or 54 years, or 9 years, or 3.5 years apart. These are cycles of hemlines, droughts, marriages, crops, plane crashes, epidemics, murders, stock market prices, tree growth, wars, new construction, etc.\nBut right now, those peaks are converging - this year will have the largest number of every type of event - a jackpot of chaos." ;
    entedit:P01 vtp:V1000 ;
    entedit:P02 entedit:T02 ;
    rdawo:P10061 per:29 .

