    rdawd:P10219 "1963" ;
    rdawd:P10330 "\"A man under medical sentence of death (a diagnosis of cancer) goes back to his childhood home and recalls there an amazing dream which he had falsified and conventionalized in a story written long ago for his school magazine. The central figure of the dream was a comic, foul-mouthed monarch of an unsuspected world 'under the garden,' which is entered by the little boy through a cave formed out of the enormous roots of an ancient tree.\" (Milton Hindus)" ;
