wrk:68361
    a rdac:C10001 ;
    rdaxd:P00018 "http://entedit.org/work/68361",
        "https://www.isfdb.org/cgi-bin/title.cgi?68361" ;
    rdawd:P10223 "As Easy As A. B. C."@en ;
    rdfs:label "As Easy As A. B. C. (Kipling, Rudyard)" ;
    rdawd:P10219 "1912-03" ;
    rdawd:P10330 "Published March to April 1912 as \"As Easy as A.B.C.\": A Tale of 2150 A.D. in The London Magazine v28, pp. 3-11, 163-71, with illustrations by F. Gardner, so signed and credited (Frederick Gardner (I) in the database).\nSources:\nForgottenFutures.com and\nThe Fiction Mags Index, which lists Contents with page numbers for vol 28, #17-18 New Series.\n(Volume 28 is not available at HathiTrust Digital Library as of 2017-10-30.)\nSequel to \"With the Night Mail\" (1905), which was lightly revised and augmented in 1909 as \"With the Night Mail: A Story of 2000 A.D. (Together with Extracts from the Contemporary Magazine in Which It Appeared)\".\nThere \"A.B.C.\" or \"ABC\" is an initialism for the Aerial Board of Control.\nSFE3 lists the 2012 collection as an expansion of the 1909 chapbook, with full title:\nWith the Night Mail and \"As Easy As ABC\": Two Yarns about the Aerial Board of Control\nand with an afterword by Bruce Sterling." ;
    entedit:P01 vtp:V1000 ;
    entedit:P02 entedit:T02 ;
    rdawo:P10061 per:1961 .

