    rdawd:P10219 "1903-10" ;
    rdawd:P10330 "Captions of the three 1903 magazine illustrations are revealing (each a quotation from the text):\n* I put out my hand, lifting my lever, turned the current into my coils, and blazed up my Y Ray for half a heart beat.\" (3 men in a laboratory setting)\n* I walked through the wall before his amazed eyes, and walked back again.\" (a displaced man occupies the same space as a wall)\n* 'Through him! Pass through him! Come out! Come to me!' I cried. (a bodily man and a displaced man occupy the same living room chair)",
        "First published October 1903 in The Metropolitan Magazine 19:1, pp. 37-47, with 3 illustrations by Lester Ralph" ;
    entedit:P01 vtp:V1000 ;
    entedit:P02 entedit:T02 ;
    rdawo:P10061 per:15689 .

