wrk:98569
    a rdac:C10001 ;
    rdaxd:P00018 "http://entedit.org/work/98569",
        "https://www.isfdb.org/cgi-bin/title.cgi?98569" ;
    rdawd:P10223 "The Toys of Peace"@en ;
    rdfs:label "The Toys of Peace (Saki)" ;
    rdawd:P10219 "1919" ;
    rdawd:P10330 "Eleanor, inspired by a newspaper article by an anti-war group, insists that her boys be given peaceful toys. But their ingenuity immediately finds ways to use the toys in war games.",
        "The newspaper article that this story satirizes actually was published in 1914. \"The Toys of Peace\" appeared in a newspaper not long after (details unknown), and was first collected in 1919.\nMarginally science-fictional in its depiction of a project to change society." ;
    entedit:P01 vtp:V1000 ;
    entedit:P02 entedit:T02 ;
    rdawo:P10061 per:1204 .

wrk:98570
    a rdac:C10001 ;
    rdaxd:P00018 "http://entedit.org/work/98570",
        "https://www.isfdb.org/cgi-bin/title.cgi?98570" ;
    rdawd:P10223 "A White Heron"@en ;
    rdfs:label "A White Heron (Jewett, Sarah Orne)" ;
    rdawd:P10219 "1886" ;
    rdawd:P10330 "Sylvia loves the natural world of her Maine home. So she's troubled when a young hunter comes and says he wants to shoot the wonderful white heron she's seen in the marshes. But since she has a crush on him, and he's offering a lot of money for her to guide him, she climbs to the top of a vey tall tree to try to spot the heron.",
        "Published in The White Heron and Other Stories, \"18[?]mo, pp. 254. Gilt top. Houghton, Mifflin & Co. $1.25\".\nThe quoted listing is from \"Books of the Month\", ''The Dial'' 1886-10 p138 under \"Fiction--Humor\", a complete list of new books received during September by Chicago publisher-wholesaler A.C. McClurg & Co.\nLCCN 07009732 links digital copies at HathiTrust; one copy from University of Michigan is dated 1886.\nThe speculative part of the story is that after Sylvia (note the name: \"of the woods\") has another transformative sight of the heron, she finds to her own surprise that she literally can't speak to tell anyone about it." ;
    entedit:P01 vtp:V1000 ;
    entedit:P02 entedit:T02 ;
    rdawo:P10061 per:17481 .

