wrk:954488
    a rdac:C10001 ;
    rdaxd:P00018 "http://entedit.org/work/954488",
        "https://www.isfdb.org/cgi-bin/title.cgi?954488" ;
    rdawd:P10223 "Уравнения Максвелла"@ru ;
    rdawd:P10086 "Uravneniya Maksvella" ;
    rdfs:label "Уравнения Максвелла (Анатолий Днепров)" ;
    rdawd:P10219 "1960-04-27" ;
    rdawd:P10330 "Narrator, a West-German professor responds to an advertisement offering scientific computations and other work. These turn out to be fast and complex beyond current possibilities – made by lunatic asylum inmates, their brains stimulated, brainwashed and ultimately destroyed by electromagnetic waves, each frequency evoking a particular emotion or function. Abducted as well, he turns the tables on their ex-Nazi captors with some applied mathematics and strength of will.",
        "First appeared in newspaper Molodaya gvardiya (published thrice weekly in Perm), issues 38–51, 27 March to 27 April 1960, and almost simultaneously in Dneprov's debut collection of the same name as the story.\nCca 13.7k words / 90.7k characters.\nPlural title \"Уравнения Максвелла\" is more widespread, and the text contains only this plural form. However singular variant of the title \"Уравнение (Uravnenie) Максвелла\" appears in some sources (Fantlab even takes it as primary) and was used at least in Dneprov's 1965 coll Purpurnaya mumiya." ;
    entedit:P01 vtp:V1000 ;
    entedit:P02 entedit:T02 ;
    rdawo:P10061 per:17078 .

