<http://viaf.org/viaf/305922109>
    a rdac:C10001 ;
    rdaxd:P00018 "http://entedit.org/work/3571",
        "https://www.isfdb.org/cgi-bin/title.cgi?3571",
        "http://viaf.org/viaf/305922109" ;
    rdawd:P10223 "Crash"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Crash (Ballard, J. G.)" ;
    rdawd:P10219 "1973-06" ;
    entedit:P01 vtp:V1000 ;
    entedit:P02 ntsf:258 ;
    rdawo:P10061 <http://viaf.org/viaf/9842556> ;
    rdawd:P10330 "In this hallucinatory novel, an automobile provides the hellish tableau in which Vaughan, a \"TV scientist\" turned \"nightmare angel of the highways,\" experiments with erotic atrocities among auto crash victims, each more sinister than the last. James Ballard, his friend and fellow obsessive, tells the story of this twisted visionary as he careens rapidly toward his own demise in an internationally orchestrated car crash with Elizabeth Taylor." .

